# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build context for the images built from the REPOSITORY ROOT:
#   apps/backend/Dockerfile
#   apps/frontend/Dockerfile
#
# Without this file the daemon receives the entire working tree on every
# build - which here means node_modules, a multi-gigabyte Python virtualenv
# holding torch, a live PostgreSQL data directory, and the .env files with the
# real signing secrets in them. Two of those are slow; the last one is a leak,
# because `COPY apps/backend apps/backend` in the backend build stage would
# otherwise place apps/backend/.env inside an image layer.
#
# Everything listed here is either reproduced inside the image from a lockfile
# or has no business in one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- version control -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# --- dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
# Reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json, so the host copy is
# both redundant and wrong (it may hold platform-specific binaries built for
# Windows).
node_modules
**/node_modules

# The pose service's virtualenv. Several gigabytes once torch is in it, and
# no Node build has any use for it.
services/pose-service/.venv

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.vite
**/.eslintcache

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example files are documentation and are NOT matched by these patterns,
# so they still reach the context.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.development
**/.env.production

# --- local database artefacts ---------------------------------------------
# .pgdata is a live PostgreSQL cluster created by the embedded-postgres
# fallback; .pgdump holds real row data and role passwords.
apps/backend/.pgdata
apps/backend/.pgdump
**/pgdata

# --- Python bytecode / caches ---------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# --- superseded prototypes -------------------------------------------------
# Kept in the repository as submitted coursework; not part of any image.
legacy
FYP

# --- not needed at build time ---------------------------------------------
docs
tools
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
Caddyfile
*.bat

# --- editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
**/*.swp

# --- logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
logs
**/*.log
